# HuntSpill-7-spill-carry.patch (lane HuntSpill, 2026-10-30; the synced tree with every patch in sync/ORDER applied):
# OTS 0123's gated carry (docs/notes/tier-carry-2026-10-10.md; TTFT map lever 2: 17.3% of all TTFT seconds in the
# 10-08/10 window) on upstream's spill blocks, which the synced base adopted in place of our tier. The spill folder is
# keyed by the build and every agreed setting (PARALLEL among them), so a restart onto a new image or setting found
# none of the agents' stored states. Now:
# - the store writes its key by parts (<folder>/rank<r>/key.json: format, block, world, rank, this rank's weights id and
#   the signature's parts by name: engine, build, drafter, kv, dense, tp, planes, grid, drafts, agreed[, kvshard]);
#   joined they are the signature the folder was always named by, so every existing folder keeps its name;
# - the gate (python3 -m tensorfold.cuda.spill_carry, in the NEW image): plan / keys / ids / check / grant / status;
#   check compares a state the new image re-prefilled with the old folder's copy byte for byte (ids, every block's
#   bytes, every small-state tensor, the head row when the old state kept one, drafter_end / mtp_len; only the lineage
#   and the bookkeeping field ``after`` may differ); grant writes carry/spill-<old>.grant.json only when every checked
#   state is equal and the two keys differ in build / agreed ALONE (spill_blocks.CARRY_PARTS);
# - the store takes a grant at start and on a quiet writer every TF_GLM_SPILL_CARRY_POLL_S (10 s; 0: start only) after
#   checking it names this folder's key and an old folder of this root and rank by name whose key is the one checked,
#   that the keys may carry, and that every checked state still has the ids and block CRC-32s / digests the gate saw;
#   then links the old folder's whole points in (load_point: the start's own check, shared now), newest first while
#   they fit the cap, blocks first and the json last, keeping their file times (the cap drops them first); a block name
#   held with other bytes, or ids held or being written, keep a point out. Refused grants are renamed .refused.json
#   (counted: carry_refused); taken ones .done.json (carried). Each rank decides alone: a point carried on some ranks
#   only is never read (HAS).
# Not here: the multi-node driver that samples the states every rank holds, replays them through the serve and runs
# check / grant on every node (tier_carry_gate.py's role for 0123); the node commands are in the lane's REPORT.md.
# Test: test_spill_carry.py <tree> (CPU torch, Linux): a state written under key A is found and loads byte-identical
# under key B after the gate granted on an equal re-prefill; one byte of a block or one recurrence value different:
# DIFF, no grant, nothing carried; a forged grant across plane shapes and a grant whose checked state changed since
# are refused by the store; B's folder name is the joined signature's (the pre-patch tree: FAIL, no key by parts).
